\ Reference checks for year-5000 candidate rules, before enumeration.
\ They test the interval boundary, minimum spans, duration bounds,
\ and both parts of the canonical length/earlier-opening sorting rule.

The year candidate test day is a calendar day.

To check year candidate eligibility:
  Put -15055671 into the year candidate test day.
  Put -15057000 into the first candidate's opening day.
  Put -15054000 into the first candidate's closing day.
  Put -3 into the first candidate's opening index.
  Put 5 into the first candidate's closing index.
  Measure the first candidate.
  If the first candidate's year length is not 3000,
    put "Year length measurement failed." into the check report; exit.
  If the first candidate's span count is not 8,
    put "Year gate-span measurement failed." into the check report; exit.
  Evaluate native year containment given the first candidate and the year candidate test day.
  If the native year containment result is not 1,
    put "Eligible candidate was incorrectly rejected." into the check report; exit.
  Put -15057000 into the year candidate test day.
  Evaluate native year containment given the first candidate and the year candidate test day.
  If the native year containment result is 1,
    put "Opening-day boundary was wrongly included." into the check report; exit.
  Put -15054000 into the year candidate test day.
  Evaluate native year containment given the first candidate and the year candidate test day.
  If the native year containment result is not 1,
    put "Closing-day boundary was wrongly excluded." into the check report; exit.
  Put -15055671 into the year candidate test day.
  Put 2 into the first candidate's closing index.
  Measure the first candidate.
  Evaluate native year containment given the first candidate and the year candidate test day.
  If the native year containment result is 1,
    put "Candidate with only five gate spans was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Put 5 into the first candidate's closing index.
  Put -15051221 into the first candidate's closing day.
  Measure the first candidate.
  Evaluate native year containment given the first candidate and the year candidate test day.
  If the native year containment result is 1,
    put "Candidate exceeding 5778 days was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Put -15055771 into the first candidate's opening day.
  Put -15055521 into the first candidate's closing day.
  Measure the first candidate.
  Evaluate native year containment given the first candidate and the year candidate test day.
  If the native year containment result is 1,
    put "Candidate shorter than 252 days was accepted." into the check report; exit.

To check year candidate order:
  Put -15057000 into the first candidate's opening day.
  Put -15054000 into the first candidate's closing day.
  Put -3 into the first candidate's opening index.
  Put 5 into the first candidate's closing index.
  Measure the first candidate.
  Put -15056800 into the second candidate's opening day.
  Put -15054200 into the second candidate's closing day.
  Put -3 into the second candidate's opening index.
  Put 6 into the second candidate's closing index.
  Measure the second candidate.
  Evaluate native year ordering given the second candidate and the first candidate.
  If the native year ordering result is not 1,
    put "The shorter eligible candidate was not first." into the check report; exit.
  Evaluate native year ordering given the first candidate and the second candidate.
  If the native year ordering result is 1,
    put "The longer eligible candidate was wrongly first." into the check report; exit.
  Put -15057100 into the second candidate's opening day.
  Put -15054100 into the second candidate's closing day.
  Measure the second candidate.
  Evaluate native year ordering given the second candidate and the first candidate.
  If the native year ordering result is not 1,
    put "Earlier opening gate did not win the length tie." into the check report; exit.
  Evaluate native year ordering given the first candidate and the second candidate.
  If the native year ordering result is 1,
    put "Later opening gate wrongly won the length tie." into the check report; exit.
